{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.chainCarrier_joins_consecutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.chainCarrier_joins_consecutive","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.lean#L166-L170","doc":"…and its `joins` really does hold somewhere — the consecutive pairs are joined,\nso the separation result above is cutting something out rather than describing an\nempty relation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.chainCarrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.chainCarrier","kind":"def","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.lean#L156-L164","doc":"**The statement is not vacuous**: a configuration satisfying every hypothesis\nexists, with `joins` inhabited on the consecutive pairs it is supposed to be\ninhabited on. Recorded so `minSpan_separated` cannot be read as holding because\nnothing can satisfy `PathCarrier`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.minSpan_separated","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.minSpan_separated","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.lean#L143-L154","doc":"**Applied to the carrier.** Every min-span triple is separated, hence carries\n`μ̄ = 0`. Independently measured on the braid words themselves: **0** generators\njoin two members of any `{i, i+2, i+4}` triple, on A = 8, 10, 12, 16 — and that\nmeasurement is branch-independent, since which components a generator touches is\nfixed by the permutation, not by how the superposition letters resolve. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.PathCarrier.lk_zero_of_not_adjacent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.PathCarrier.lk_zero_of_not_adjacent","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.lean#L141-L141","doc":"non-consecutive components are unlinked ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.PathCarrier.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.PathCarrier.mk","kind":"ctor","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.lean#L139-L139","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.PathCarrier.toSummands","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.PathCarrier.toSummands","kind":"def","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.lean#L139-L141","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.PathCarrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.PathCarrier","kind":"structure","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.lean#L136-L141","doc":"The path carrier: `lk` vanishes off consecutive pairs. Stated as the direction\nactually used — non-adjacent implies unlinked — rather than as an `iff`, so the\ntheorem below does not silently require more than the measurement supports. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.minSpan_pairwise_not_adjacent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.minSpan_pairwise_not_adjacent","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.lean#L128-L134","doc":"**The min-span family is pairwise non-adjacent.** `{i, i+2, i+4}` is the\ntightest triple with this property, which is why `qou-768r` names it: it is the\nsmallest family that is Milnor-*defined*, and it is the only one whose count\n(`A − 3`, per-component multiplicity ≤ 3) survives `CoordinationSaturation`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.instDecidableAdjacent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.instDecidableAdjacent","kind":"instance","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.lean#L123-L126","doc":"`Adjacent` is a disjunction of `ℕ`-equalities, so it decides — but the `def`\nopaques it to instance synthesis, which is what the witness below needs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.Adjacent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.Adjacent","kind":"def","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.lean#L119-L121","doc":"Adjacency on the path `P_μ` that the derived carrier's linking graph is\nmeasured to be: `lk ≠ 0` exactly on consecutive components. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.separated_of_delta_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.separated_of_delta_zero","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.lean#L100-L117","doc":"**The result, and it is the whole file.** A triple on which `μ̄` is a genuine\ninteger — `Δ = gcd(lk_ij, lk_jk, lk_ki) = 0`, i.e. all three pairwise linking\nnumbers vanish — shares **no** summand between any two of its members.\n\nIts sublink is therefore **split**, and every Milnor invariant of length ≥ 2 vanishes\non a split link — whatever the individual components are knotted as (measured: they\nare `(2, odd)`-torus knots, not unknots; local knotting changes no Milnor invariant). So on this carrier the condition that makes `μ̄` *defined* is the condition\nthat makes it *zero*.\n\nNeeds no path structure, no minimality, and no `Δ`-arithmetic: it is exactly the\ncontrapositive of `joins_linked`, which is why the result is as general as the\nconnected-sum decomposition itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.Summands.joins_linked","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.Summands.joins_linked","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.lean#L98-L98","doc":"sharing a summand makes two components linked ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.Summands.lk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.Summands.lk","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.lean#L96-L96","doc":"linking numbers of the closure ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.Summands.joins","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.Summands.joins","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.lean#L94-L94","doc":"some summand of the connected sum touches both components ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.Summands.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.Summands.mk","kind":"ctor","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.lean#L92-L92","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.Summands","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.Summands","kind":"structure","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorTriplesAreDefinedExactlyWhereTheyVanish.lean#L85-L98","doc":"Two components are **joined** when some summand of the connected-sum\ndecomposition touches both.\n\nOn the derived carrier a summand is one generator's run, so it touches only the\ncomponents containing strands `g` and `g+1` — measured at most two, on\nA = 2, 4, 6, 8, 10. The single hypothesis `joins_linked` is what the topology\nsupplies: a shared `(2, k)` torus summand links the two components it joins. ","signatureChunk":0}]}